        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/goal.node-class.node",
        "owner": "Michael",
        "body": "A node, an edge, a handle and a graph each has a panel built from one contract, so a switch is described once and every reader (the panel, a template, an agent) reads the same description.",
        "status": "in-progress",
        "successMetrics": [
          "The contract covers node, edge, handle and graph switches, each with where it is written, its default, its valid values and where it applies.",
          "Every switch has a control, or a stated reason it does not.",
          "Advanced is a last resort, not the way to set a switch.",
          "The old type tables, legacy payload keys and per-browser style presets are gone.",
          "The Properties panel is no longer one 6,200-line component."
        ],
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1792950744123,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        },
        "notes": "2026-10-25: the five questions are answered (four scopes, selectable handles, graph panel on empty selection, a versioned schema the panel reads, the contract published in canon). Next: Schema v1, then the panels."
      }
