      "data": {
        "title": "Is data.switch a reference agents read, or a schema the app reads and validates?",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "properties-and-authoring-contract",
          "nodeId": "properties-and-authoring-contract-q-schema"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/open-question.node-class.node",
        "owner": "Michael",
        "status": "answered",
        "body": "A reference costs nothing and the test already holds its shape. A schema means a loader, a version and a validator, and is only worth it if the panel is built from it.\n\nDecision: Make data.switch a versioned, validated, machine-readable authoring schema, not merely agent documentation. The Properties panel is its first consumer; templates and agents read the same definitions. It specifies scope, type, default, valid values, write path and applicability. Runtime code still implements behaviors. Build incrementally rather than making the schema a programming language.",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1792950744125,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    },
