      "data": {
        "title": "Schema v1: the four scopes, a version, and a validator",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "properties-and-authoring-contract",
          "nodeId": "properties-and-authoring-contract-schema"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/task.node-class.node",
        "owner": "Michael",
        "status": "done",
        "body": "Decided: data.switch is a versioned, validated, machine-readable schema, built incrementally and not a programming language. Today scope mixes four authoring scopes (node, edge, handle, graph) with the kinds a switch applies to (face, port, root, method). Split them: `scope` is one of the four, `appliesTo` names the kinds. Add a schema version and a pure validator (a small module, with tests); move the 21 switches to it. Runtime code still implements behaviour.",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1792986466257,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        },
        "notes": "Schema v1 is components/GraphEditor/utils/authoringContract.js: four scopes (node, edge, handle, graph), appliesTo for the kinds inside a scope, value types, modes, a validator, and switchesFor / switchAtPath. The 21 switches moved onto it; the validator caught renderShape (it is the content format, not an outline, and now lists its values)."
      }
    },
